# passages/00089-Immortality.mws.yaml
Immortality_001=Overcoming Death
Immortality_002=If not now, then when? The cousins pored over this question. How long would they remain relegated to an eccentric footnote murmured amongst the townspeople? Why must they toil in their most important labors under the cover of darkness and stone like vermin? A deep restlessness had set into the minds of each, and even on the cusp of approval from the academic community, they could not quell these thoughts.
Immortality_003=It was trivial to discuss meager experimentations when the solidification of such a poignant legacy repeated fruitlessly generation upon generation. If only time was no longer an obstacle.
Immortality_004=They vowed to accumulate a wealth of knowledge in their fields of expertise that far surpassed the pitiable ruminations of ancient scholars. Perhaps if they pushed forward into the unknown they would harness new and untold powers. Their evening conversations spurred them to devise a way to cheat the most sacred and inevitable truth of existence.
Immortality_005=For if life can be taken and altered by humanity into its most cruel and twisted form, surely that same spark could be endlessly preserved!

# passages/00091-DetEffect1.mws.yaml
DetEffect1_001=Major Deleterious Effect
DetEffect1_002=It could not continue. Sick and unable to heal again, stumbling blindly until the bones were brittle enough to snap, their bodies had finally failed them. And when the mind had joined the fragile physical form in its inability to perform the most basic of functions, the struggle ceased.
DetEffect1_003=Death in all its inevitability had finally claimed them.
DetEffect1_004=Unfortunately, their body was in such an advanced state of degradation it could not even be used for further experimentation. This made the grief more substantial.
DetEffect1_006=Any player with an **Immortality card** discards a **Caretaker** to Lost.
DetEffect1_007=Discard all **Immortality cards** to the scenario box.

# passages/00092-DetEffect2.mws.yaml
DetEffect2_002=They feared that their hasty solution had borne upon them irreversible effects. The interior withered, the skin grayed and sagged translucently against the sinewy veins beneath. The ultimate cure had become a curse and life was like a festering wound that cut deeper with each passing day. Still, they continued on in their work, hoping the effects were temporary but fearing the worst. It took more and more resources to quell their pain each day.
DetEffect2_003=Any player with an **Immortality card** discards an **Ingredient** _if possible_ and **draws a Compulsion**.

# passages/00093-DetEffect3.mws.yaml
DetEffect3_001=All and all, the continued effects of their approach to Immortality had fared exceptionally well. While the skin displayed liver spots and an amount of vigor had been lost as the blood cooled with age, the effects were only a distraction. At most, a gangrenous finger had to be excised once every few years, but what was one extraneous extremity compared to the ability to assist in the most important scientific discoveries the world had ever known?
DetEffect3_002=Any player with an **Immortality card** loses **{_rnd_DetEffect3_0}VP**.

# passages/00094-DetEffect4.mws.yaml
DetEffect4_001=No Effect
DetEffect4_002=The unthinkable had been achieved. Whether by sheer providence or remarkable display of intellect, the solution to immortality appeared to have worked! In fact, the effects were so remarkable that many witness accounts of the day observed that the aging process appeared to have reversed. While still aged by all accounts, their individual treatise on Immortality appeared to have succeeded.
DetEffect4_003=At least, for now.

# passages/00095-InfinityClick2.mws.yaml
InfinityClick2_001=Secret to
InfinityClick2_002=Marvelous
InfinityClick2_003=Discovering
InfinityClick2_004=Forward to
