# passages/00100-S5HospA1No.mws.yaml
S5HospA1No_001=Death Becomes Us
S5HospA1No_002=As their bodies withered with time, the failures of their equally outdated scientific pursuits weighed heavily on their deteriorating minds. With only **{life}** of them discovering the way towards **immortality**, the cousins wallowed in their own ineptitude.
S5HospA1No_003=With no further push from its energetic benefactors, the university was shunned, abandoned, and refitted. 
S5HospA1No_004=With no sounds of screams and explosions echoing down from the hillsides, the townsfolk lost their sense of purpose. A thick fog of ignorance fell across the populace as they returned to the old ways with a righteous fervor.
S5HospA1No_005=Click to continue to a more depressing time...

# passages/00101-DevEventCure.mws.yaml
DevEventCure_001=An Alternative Cure
DevEventCure_002=An envoy from the 
DevEventCure_005= arrived bearing an interesting narrative and a shimmering tincture of liquid. She visited each of the manors in turn unable to conceal her wicked grin and laughter as she did so.
DevEventCure_006="The brotherhood has heard of your suffering and we wish to offer an exchange. For a meager bit of knowledge, we present a cure. Drink of this liquid and your dreaded affliction will cease," she said as a bolt of lightning arced across the sky above.
DevEventCure_007=Each player, in turn order, may choose to discard a completed B-Level Experiment _(to the bottom of the deck)_ to place their **Hereditary Disease Experiment** into their **Stored Experiments**. _They will no longer be affected by Disease events._
DevEventCure_008=Any player that has already completed their **Hereditary Disease Experiment** cannot choose this action.
DevEventCure_009=Continue once all players have made their decision.

