# passages/00104-Diseases1.mws.yaml
Diseases1_001=**A Year of Sickness**
Diseases1_002=Even the most agile mind cannot willingly escape the frailness of the human form. As such, the foul plague upon the household syphoned a considerable energy from their work and left them bed-ridden for months on end. 
Diseases1_003=All players that have not completed the **Hereditary Disease Experiment** must **discard a Knowledge cube to the supply** or **lose 2VP**.
Diseases1_004=**Rest and Time**
Diseases1_005=It seemed that the cousins were fortunate in their early years. Even the most agile mind cannot willingly escape the frailness of the human form. However, with a strict regimen of rest, diet, and bloodletting, these deficiencies could mostly be nullified.
Diseases1_006=The Hereditary disease has no effect.

# passages/00105-HubertusWolves3.mws.yaml
HubertusWolves3_001=**Upon a Secret Meeting - Letter - {_rnd_HubertusWolves3_0} {_rnd_HubertusWolves3_1}, 1865**

# passages/00106-HubertusHunters1.mws.yaml
HubertusHunters1_001=**Upon a Secret Meeting - Letter - {_rnd_HubertusHunters1_0} {_rnd_HubertusHunters1_1}, 1865**
HubertusHunters1_004=amusingly exploitative. The Fraternity hopes to use the recent epidemic as a cover for their activities to unearth ancient supernatural secrets in the region and use them for monetary and political gain. Although I remain skeptical, if these labors are successful, I will be deeply interested in the results. You only asked for your work to remain **concealed**.

# passages/00107-DevastationFate1.mws.yaml
DevastationFate1_001=Strong Alliance
DevastationFate1_002=Remove all player pieces from the board and Perform the End of a Generation. Return any remaining {icon:storybook} tokens to the supply.
DevastationFate1_003=The ties that bound the family to these secret warring factions changed the course of history.
DevastationFate1_004=By exposing the insidious deeds of the **Fraternity of Hunters,** the additional attention forced them to quit the region. Motivated by the promise of swift justice, the **Order of St. Hubertus** created a stronghold in the town. They swore to provide a haven for all outcasts.
DevastationFate1_005=While secrets could not forever be kept, the silent assistance of {playtxt} influential members of the upper crust ensured that the **Order** could progress in their endeavors long enough to make their presence integral to the town. They immediately began to advance their schemes.
DevastationFate1_006=By exposing the nefarious work of the **Order of St. Hubertus,** the additional attention forced them to leave the region. Motivated by the promise of swift justice, the **Fraternity of Hunters** created a stronghold in the town. They swore at all costs to protect the town from the evils that roamed the land.
DevastationFate1_007=While secrets could not forever be kept, the silent assistance of {playtxt} influential members of the upper crust ensured that the **Hunters** could progress in their endeavors long enough to make their presence integral to the town. For a price, they swore to protect all citizens from the disease and darkness that had enveloped the countryside.

