# passages/00122-Trigger35Points.mws.yaml
Trigger35Points_001=**Carefully hand this storybook device to the player that just reached 35VP. This is read within view of all players.**
Trigger35Points_002=**"Unfortunate Accident" - Journal Entry, 1876**
Trigger35Points_003=My work! My property! Sabotaged.
Trigger35Points_004=I awoke this evening to find my home on fire and the culprits nowhere to be found. But, I know who did it. I could still smell the chemical reaction as the fires raged. I would have never expected my cousins to stoop to such a base level. Direct and blatant sabotage? Absolutely unconscionable.
Trigger35Points_005=It will take weeks for my spouse to manage the removal of the damaged piece of our Estate. They are all just jealous of my genius!
Trigger35Points_006=**"Nasty Rumors" - Journal Entry, 1878**
Trigger35Points_007=To reach the pinnacle of understanding, only to feel the cruel hand of treachery. The rest of the family was noticeably not distraught when a recent article in the regional newspaper spread an uncomfortable rumor about my personal hygiene.
Trigger35Points_008=I do not have time for this interruption! I do not smell like pickles! It is the formaldehyde solution for my most recent experiment. It is not the smell of pickles; it is the smell of SCIENCE!
Trigger35Points_009=Immediately **lose 4VP** and **discard an Estate Upgrade of your choice**.
Trigger35Points_010=Immediately **gain 2** {icon:creepy_icon} and **gain 1** {icon:insanity_icon}.

# passages/00123-Trigger3Experiments.mws.yaml
Trigger3Experiments_002=Please click on the name of the scientist that completed a total of **3 B or C {sci3} Experiments**:

# passages/00124-ChooseScience.mws.yaml
ChooseScience_001=**Carefully hand the Storybook to {charity}. This choice is read and made within view of all players.**
ChooseScience_002=**"Universal Interest" - Journal Entry - November, 1859 - {charity}**
ChooseScience_003=It has been three days since I received a letter from the Hungarian government and two days since my cousins deigned it necessary to make me the target of their ridicule. My parents cared deeply for this horrid community - a sentiment that those miscreants know nothing about!
ChooseScience_004=I am not some groveler who needs confirmation from the stuffed shirts and upturned noses of European academies. But, getting to choose the **subject of the upcoming Symposium** that could very well determine if a **University** is built in {townname}?
ChooseScience_005=My parents instilled into me a scientific vigor that far surpasses even the members of my own, somewhat beloved, family. As I returned from studies abroad, it was my own aptitudes that spearheaded my cousins into action. Damn them and their jibes! I will show them. In fact, I have already made my choice and penned my response. It will be I who will be doing the laughing in the end.
ChooseScience_006=**Choose which of the Sciences our family will focus upon this Generation:**

# passages/00125-SymposiumEvent1.mws.yaml
SymposiumEvent1_001=A Collection of Esteemed Colleagues
SymposiumEvent1_002=The journey to the newly created city of Budapest for the {sci3} Symposium was uncharacteristically dour. However, this dreadful murkiness could not dampen the spirits of the {playtxt}; nor could the sojourn in the marginal accommodations prepared for their arrival. For the cousins, this recognition for their efforts to advance science at all costs was considerably well-deserved and long-overdue.
SymposiumEvent1_003=The University was abuzz with activity as they attended various events and offered their prescribed greetings.

# passages/00127-SanityChoice.mws.yaml
SanityChoice_001=**Carefully hand the Storybook to {saneplayer}. This choice is read and made within view of all players.**
SanityChoice_002=**Journal Entry, {saneplayer} - September, 1892**
SanityChoice_003=The fools! The utter fools! In their haste to return to their amateurish attempts at science, my dear, witless cousins have been overlooked by our colleagues at the university. And so it fell to me to advise them on this most important psychological matter!
SanityChoice_004=My in-depth studies of phrenology and first-hand observation of brain function have allowed me to calculate with flawless accuracy the appropriate level of mental intensity needed to excel in science; the most proper balance of passion and ethical ambiguity.
SanityChoice_005=While, yes, we may ALL benefit from this assessment and yes, they did only consult me out of a sense of pity, it is I alone that will now control the fate of us all!
SanityChoice_007={saneplayer} must now choose a numbered spot below on the {icon:insanity_icon} Track.
SanityChoice_008=At the end of the Generation, any player whose piece is on this space will **gain 5VP**.
SanityChoice_009=4
SanityChoice_010=5
SanityChoice_011=6
SanityChoice_012=7

# passages/00128-LycanthropicMessage.mws.yaml
LycanthropicMessage_001=The Form of the Wolf
LycanthropicMessage_002=Confirming the existence of individuals with the ability to change into an animal form had remarkable consequences. It is possible that it has even disrupted the studies of one of our kin.

# passages/00129-LycanEvil.mws.yaml
LycanEvil_002=Their existence was proven. Now, could the catalyst of this truly powerful transformation be replicated? And how could it be further strengthened?

# passages/00130-HospitalVisitCheck.mws.yaml
HospitalVisitCheck_001=A Compulsory Visitation
HospitalVisitCheck_002=The {townname} General Hospital was one of the first hospitals in the region. Established in 1865, it was instrumental in changing the public perception of a hospital from a place you go to die to a place of healing with the most modern advances in medicine.
HospitalVisitCheck_003=On the day of the visit, several nurses bandied about, treating patients from nearby villages with symptoms of the Yellow Fever
HospitalVisitCheck_004= and using the innoculation techniques that the family had recently published
HospitalVisitCheck_005=Click on the name of the player **visiting the Hospital** today:

# passages/00131-HospitalVisitCheck2.mws.yaml
HospitalVisitCheck2_001=**Visitation Report: Dr. {hospsign} - Notes submitted by Nurse Varga**
HospitalVisitCheck2_002=Relatively uneventful visit, though unsettling. Dr. {hospsign} requested a tour through the wards.
HospitalVisitCheck2_003=At one juncture, Dr. {hospsign} approached a patient in the hallway that had been confined to a bath chair. Unprompted, they began a through examination of the individual, palpating their hairline and skull with their fingers. To my dismay, they were enraptured by a rash along the patients cheek which was covered in small protusions and red boils. They insisted on collecting several samples of the fluid they produced.
HospitalVisitCheck2_004=Mostly disinterested and silent. However, our visit to the morgue was longer than to my liking. Dr. {hospsign} kept insisting on inspecting the more extreme cases, excitedly asking questions while I unsuccessfully attempted to stop them from physically handling the deceased.
HospitalVisitCheck2_005=After requesting access to more severe emergency cases, we walked the grounds. They kept stating that the facilities were "unimpressive compared to their own." I shudder to think on what that phrase means.
HospitalVisitCheck2_006=Dr. {hospsign} seemed in a hurry. Dismissed each area as sterile and uninspired. Until we arrived at the operating room. Immediately became enraptured, fixated, and I had to thrice repeat myself before they responded.
HospitalVisitCheck2_007=Their response was muffled and I was unable to stop them from entering the theater. Their face was etched in a hideous grin as they stood at the center with their hands raised into the air. At this point, they either refused to listen or entered a catatonic state which left them motionless for nearly an hour.
HospitalVisitCheck2_008="This is all wrong. What do they teach in these surgeon schools?" Dr. {hospsign} asked, clearly not expecting an answer and brazenly entered the operating room to accost the surgeons on duty. They retrieved a scalpel and insisting on completing the operation themselves. I have never seen so much blood.
HospitalVisitCheck2_009=At this point, {hospsign} had to be escorted by security from the premises. They are barred from any further tours of the facilities.

# passages/00132-HospitalNegative.mws.yaml
HospitalNegative_001=**Lack of Hospitality**
HospitalNegative_002=Unfortunately, the lack of participation in the Hospital Board of Trustees needed to be reckoned and any who chose to forgo their obligations felt their business dealings in the local area become even further strained.
HospitalNegative_003=Dr. {nameA} Jr. must immediately lose 6VP and discard an Estate Upgrade of their choice.
HospitalNegative_004=Dr. {nameB} Jr. must immediately lose 6VP and discard an Estate Upgrade of their choice.
HospitalNegative_005=Dr. {nameC} Jr. must immediately lose 6VP and discard an Estate Upgrade of their choice.
HospitalNegative_006=Dr. {nameD} Jr. must immediately lose 6VP and discard an Estate Upgrade of their choice.
HospitalNegative_007=Dr. {nameE} Jr. must immediately lose 6VP and discard an Estate Upgrade of their choice.

