# passages/00177-Gen1-CreepyTrack.mws.yaml
Gen1_CreepyTrack_001=Enemy of the People
Gen1_CreepyTrack_002=The increasingly eccentric actions of the siblings aroused dark memories from the previous generation, and tense rumors once again circulated throughout the village. However, as these same fears were shared more openly, the news attracted opportunities for those with similar, nefarious intent.
Gen1_CreepyTrack_003=Please click on the name of the scientist that reached **space 4** on the {icon:creepy_icon} track:

# passages/00178-Gen1-SanityTrack.mws.yaml
Gen1_SanityTrack_001=To Quell the Mind
Gen1_SanityTrack_002=Just as a sharpened blade loses some of its steel, so it is the same with a pointed intellect so repeatedly ground. This precise focus upon scientific labors caused the siblings' brains to wander and ache for relief even as a powerful ambition compelled them well beyond their physical tolerances.
Gen1_SanityTrack_003=Please click on the name of the scientist that reached **space 3** on the {icon:insanity_icon} track:

# passages/00179-Gen1-CreepyTrackRes.mws.yaml
Gen1_CreepyTrackRes_001=A Seedy Arrangement
Gen1_CreepyTrackRes_003=It was unorthodox for {gen1creep}, or anyone of that reclusive lineage, to entertain unknown visitors, but something must have piqued their curiosity. A conversation from an evening dinner is noted in a journal entry:
Gen1_CreepyTrackRes_004="Your reputation is known across the region for vehemently challenging the established norms," the representative from the Order of St. Hubertus was noted as saying with a wide grin. They leaned in conspiratorially, an expensive perfume loud enough in fragrance to draw water from the eyes. "From what I hear, you are unwilling to allow the rules of academia to hold your work back from its true excellence. Please, let me admire your experimentation."
Gen1_CreepyTrackRes_005=This was highly controversial! And to be so brazen about it! It was left to the scientist to decide if being granted the opportunity to **perform an extra experiment** was worth the possible consequences of revealing one's work.
Gen1_CreepyTrackRes_006=Accept.
Gen1_CreepyTrackRes_007=(To take a Perform Experiment Action.)
Gen1_CreepyTrackRes_008=Refuse.
Gen1_CreepyTrackRes_009=(If you cannot or choose not to take the action.)
Gen1_CreepyTrackRes_010="Your estate is simply exquisite," the representative was noted as saying with an unsettling grin. "I am impressed to find a rarefied jewel nestled in such a remote place. But, as you will no doubt agree, it can always use improvement and I would like to offer you support in this." In fact, it was noted that the individual's mannerisms were especially secretive and plotting.
Gen1_CreepyTrackRes_011=The representative from the Fraternity of Hunters offered their support with substantial funds. With the "hope" that this kindness would be repaid in the future.
Gen1_CreepyTrackRes_012=Accept the offer.
Gen1_CreepyTrackRes_013=(To gain $2.)
Gen1_CreepyTrackRes_014=Refuse the offer.
Gen1_CreepyTrackRes_015=(To avoid a debt in the future.)

# passages/00180-Gen1-SanityTrackRes.mws.yaml
Gen1_SanityTrackRes_001=A Letter From an Old Friend
Gen1_SanityTrackRes_002=**Carefully hand this storybook device to {gen1sane} and do not allow any other players to see the screen.**
Gen1_SanityTrackRes_003="You shouldn't drive yourself so hard," the letter stated. "It is unsustainable. For each night you toil away until dawn's light, it takes years from your mind."
Gen1_SanityTrackRes_004=While the nature of their work ensured that it was performed in solitude, {gen1sane}, and their spouse especially, still enjoyed writing letters to the few friends who would receive them. This particular letter from an old colleague at university recommended a specific retreat in Rovinj, where the warm Mediterranean air would rejuvenate the body and quiet the mind. For a small price, they could own a vacation home.
Gen1_SanityTrackRes_005=While this time away could have a negative affect on their child, it would also allow them to **gain knowledge** and **calm their sanity**. Refusal, however, would carry no risk and maybe give them more time to complete their labors.
Gen1_SanityTrackRes_006=Accept the offer and pay $1. (Calm your sanity and gain 1 Knowledge.)
Gen1_SanityTrackRes_007=Refuse. (Avoid the penalties of laziness.)

# passages/00181-LycanGood.mws.yaml
LycanGood_001=Their existence was proven. Now could the catalyst for this truly powerful transformation be replicated? And how could it be further strengthened?

# passages/00182-GoodConsequences.mws.yaml
GoodConsequences_001=The Consequences of Being Good
GoodConsequences_002=The sizzle of concentrated electricity, the sounds of agonized screams, the occasional plume of putrid smoke and teeth-rattling explosion; while these sounds were commonplace to hear emanating from the hilltop residences, they were nevertheless an increasing source of tension between the family's important research and the townsfolk. And while their etiquette would never allow them to directly address the issue, the lycanthropic citizens bristled at each frightening experiment all the same.
GoodConsequences_003=The town was desperate to move forward and they could not stomach the cousins' ambitions, which only served to dredge up the weight of guilt over their tortured pasts.
GoodConsequences_004=Retrieve the {icon:creepy_icon} **tokens** from the scenario box. Each player must place a {icon:creepy_icon} token on the Perform Experiment Action in their Estate.
GoodConsequences_005=Every time a Perform Experiment Action is taken, that player will move forward 1 space on the {icon:creepy_icon} Track _(in addition to any other printed effects)_.

# passages/00183-RefusalReveal.mws.yaml
RefusalReveal_001="You do well to proceed with caution," The stable hand stated. "The situation, as I understand it, is simple. The Order of St. Hubertus is {wolves}. Fraternity of Hunters is {hunters}. It doesn't get much simpler than that, to me at least."
RefusalReveal_002="The Order - not sure what they really want per se. Something about unleashing a horrible vengeance on mankind. It isn't very specific. They want to keep their work **concealed** and are even now setting up a way to perform their **Experiments**.
RefusalReveal_003="The Order wants the village to become a haven for outcasts. They're set to **expose** the evils in the region and if they do, you can be sure they'll build a University with **skilled workers**.
RefusalReveal_004=" **Money**, power, influence. If the Fraternity can use these dark secrets to their advantage, they will. They want to **conceal** their work in the village. They prey on the weak-willed and gullible.
RefusalReveal_005=" The Fraternity; the usual good guy routine. **Expose** injustice in the village today and hunt down the demons that roam the countryside. If you want to **regain your sanity** in this messed up world, they'll be the ones to aid.
RefusalReveal_006= He punctuated his final statement with a puff of acrid tobacco.
RefusalReveal_007={meet} was fascinated by the idea of not one, but two secret societies hiding in this very village. The stable hand, after an exchange of some coin, was even willing to give instructions on how to contact the factions for membership. {meet} was presented with a curious dilemma indeed.
RefusalReveal_008=**You may choose to:**
RefusalReveal_009=Join the Order of St. Hubertus.
RefusalReveal_010=Join the Fraternity of Hunters.
RefusalReveal_011=Leave and do Nothing.

# passages/00186-EvilHunter1Event.mws.yaml
EvilHunter1Event_001=Preposterous
EvilHunter1Event_002=And how could they be sure of these claims to rid the land of monsters? Could the superstitions of {townname} have influenced their decisions so completely?
EvilHunter1Event_003=But, perhaps a sense of safety or convenience had overwhelmed the cousins' frugal disposition. Whatever their motivations, several journal entries noted that without the combined efforts of the group, refusal to pay mandated taxes would only cause undue negative attention.
EvilHunter1Event_005=All players take their Voting token into their hand. Players will secretly choose a side to place face up in their palm. Then, they will close their fist and extend it to the center of the table.
EvilHunter1Event_006=A **Yay** vote is a vote to **Challenge the Hunters** about their monster hunting claims.
EvilHunter1Event_007=A **Nay** vote is a vote to **Accept their story**.

# passages/00187-WolvesEvil1.mws.yaml
WolvesEvil1_001=A Call for Assistance
WolvesEvil1_002=Each cousin's recollection of events seems to corroborate the same story during the Summer of 1892. A messenger, obviously meant to intimidate, arrived by carriage unannounced precisely at noon, dressed in a dapper gray suit stained in thick streaks by rivulets of blood that cascaded from his shoulders. He wore a mask of gore, his animalistic features stained a sanguine red that still dripped from the tips of his teeth, his belly distending the buttons as if he had recently enjoyed a horrifying meal.
WolvesEvil1_003="I come to collect," he entreated with a bow and disgusting lick of his lips. "It is by our pleasure that you and your family remain alive. And we have need of the knowledge of experimentation that you most assuredly can provide. If this cannot be arranged," he paused, pointing in the direction of a servant, "I have slaked my thirst on the blood of lesser individuals than these today, that I guarantee."
WolvesEvil1_004=Making a deal with demons? It was impossible for the young scientists to expect an entirely trustworthy offer as presented, yet to allow a human to be knowingly sacrificed to the jaws of these grotesque animals would also be unconscionable.
WolvesEvil1_006=If a player donates, they will receive an immediate bonus based on the level of the Experiment they donate (_higher levels granting higher rewards_).

# passages/00188-DiseaseEffect.mws.yaml
DiseaseEffect_001=**Not Passed Down**
DiseaseEffect_002=Twenty years passed without incident. As they were known to state, the only true science was that which one could observe plainly to a most dizzying effect. Surely, there would have been signs of the disease resurfacing in the next generation by then if it were truly a hereditary disease.
DiseaseEffect_003=Family curse? They dismissed it as simple superstition.
DiseaseEffect_004=All players who did not complete or store their **Hereditary Disease Experiment** discard them to the scenario box.
DiseaseEffect_005=**A Continuing Malady**
DiseaseEffect_006=It appeared that the effects of the disease had been inherited by the next Generation. Without a cure, symptoms of this ailment began to surface at an early age and would carry on through the remainder of their lives.
DiseaseEffect_007=Any player who did not complete or store their Hereditary Disease Experiment draws a **Maladjustment** card for the next Generation. Then, return that Experiment to the scenario box.

# passages/00189-TaxesEventNoConfrontation.mws.yaml
TaxesEventNoConfrontation_001=Rising Cost of Living
TaxesEventNoConfrontation_002=While the townsfolk grumbled at the mention of a continuing increase in taxation, they clutched their crosses to their chests and remained thankful for the Hunters' continued vigilance. Because of their previous acquiescence, the family could no longer voice their displeasure and was forced to remunerate the Fraternity for their service if they had not done so already.
TaxesEventNoConfrontation_004=Alternatively, any player with a Hunter token **MUST** now discard it to the scenario box to invoke their privilege and forgo this payment.

# passages/00190-TaxesEventStart.mws.yaml
TaxesEventStart_001=The Hunt Begins
TaxesEventStart_002=The hunter stood upon the steps of the Hunter's Lodge, dressed in a leather trenchcoat and holding a crossbow in his left hand. His garments were speckled in fresh streaks of blood while other members of the Fraternity stood nearby in black raincoats, brandishing handaxes, pistols, and muskets, holding aloft severed trophies from monsters slain in the wilderness. They had returned from the hunt.
TaxesEventStart_003=The hunter spoke to the crowd of townspeople that had assembled, his eyes barely visible under the wide brim of his hat. "No longer will this great city be forced to endure this hardship. We, the Fraternity of Hunters, will take the fight to the beasts of the forest. It is the monsters within these very hills that brought with them a pestilence and spread their sinful disease across the land. And with your assistance, we will exterminate these vermin and drive them back to hell once again!"
TaxesEventStart_004=The speech evoked jubilant cheers from the populace and the Fraternity's dominance over the town was secured. Even a modest **tax** from the new local government to help pay for the hunter's excursions into the wilds was met without skepticism.

# passages/00191-EvilHunter1EventYes.mws.yaml
EvilHunter1EventYes_001=Prepare a Contest
EvilHunter1EventYes_002=The family underwent months of travel both by day and the pale light of the moon with barely the whisper of an ill wind or the echo of a beastly wail. It was clear to their scientific minds that these demonic occurrences were nothing more than mere flights of fancy. Without hesitance, they relayed these accusations against the **Fraternity of Hunters**.
EvilHunter1EventYes_003=After an exchange of exasperated guffaws, it was decided that the Fraternity would provide guaranteed proof of their supernatural exploits by confronting the cursed beasts of the evening in full view of the townspeople. A great festival was planned around the contest, and under the light of a blood moon they would venture into the cursed hills and return with more trophies than ever before. But, if they were successful, the scientists would owe them a debt, **with interest**.
EvilHunter1EventYes_004=The cousins agreed to the terms while also devising a most insidious plot. They chortled with undisguised laughter. If the Hunters wanted a true bounty, they would give it to them!

# passages/00192-HunterConfrontation.mws.yaml
HunterConfrontation_001=The Grand Contest
HunterConfrontation_002=April, 1902
HunterConfrontation_003=After years of apologies and unfortunate delays by the **Fraternity of Hunters**, the night of the Grand Contest had arrived. The confrontation had been touted extensively within the region and visitors gathered near the {townname} Lodge to witness the spectacle of the hunt. The Hunters were treated to a tickertape parade and glorious feast. But, as the light of the afternoon slowly faded, the sky began to glow with fiery intensity, and the revelry ceased.
HunterConfrontation_004=The Hunters donned their signature clothes, took up their well-polished arms, and proceeded down the main thoroughfare while the crimson light of the blood moon heralded their exit into the forests beyond.
HunterConfrontation_005=That same fire reflected in the eyes of the scientists as they stifled their grim laughter. The night before, the cousins had prepared their chosen Experiments to release into the wild. It was time now for the Hunters to become the prey!
HunterConfrontation_006=Click to Resolve the Event...

# passages/00193-OhYesTheyDead.mws.yaml
OhYesTheyDead_001=A "Hero's" Welcome
OhYesTheyDead_002=The cousins enjoyed fresh pastries and coffee as they admired the town's activities with amusement from their folding lawn chairs. When the triumphant return they had expected never came, the gathered crowds became restless and burst into the Hunter's Lodge only to discover stores of freshly slaughtered goat's blood and taxidermy supplies. The Fraternity had played them for fools.
OhYesTheyDead_003=The town gallows had fallen into disrepair over the years, but upon the return of the remaining wild-eyed hunters that somehow survived the vicious experiments, lumber was quickly procured by the decidedly unimpressed townsfolk along with fresh hemp rope, thick and strong. The same crowd that gathered that afternoon for the festivities would be the crowd that watched every last writhing body swing lifeless for their crimes. If any Hunters did survive, they most certainly never returned.
OhYesTheyDead_004=The people would speak of the Grand Contest as one of the crowning events in the history of {townname}. Having rooted out the evil infesting their government, the town entered a period of peace that was especially productive for a group of scientists.
OhYesTheyDead_005=The player(s) who contributed the Experiment worth the highest VP gains **{huntvp}VP**. _All tied players gain this VP._
OhYesTheyDead_006=Move the {icon:angrymob_icon} token **2 spaces** to the right.
OhYesTheyDead_007=All contributed Experiments are then discarded to the bottom of the appropriate Experiment decks.

# passages/00194-ConfrontationFail.mws.yaml
ConfrontationFail_001=A Hero's Welcome
ConfrontationFail_002=The Hunters return relatively unscathed by the proceedings to a resounding cheer from the excited crowd. Covered in blood and oil, with the trophies of their victory held high, they regaled the crowd with their highly embellished and harrowing tale. Each ferocious severed head receiving more applause than the last.
ConfrontationFail_003=For a family that until now had never been forced to admit shame, the blow was unmistakable. Disheartened and angry with their current fate, they silently immersed themselves in their labors, resolved to avoid further visits to town at all costs.
ConfrontationFail_004=**Experimental Bonus**
ConfrontationFail_005=The player(s) who contributed the Experiment worth the highest VP gains **{huntvp}**. _All tied players gain this VP._
ConfrontationFail_006=All contributed Experiments are discarded.
ConfrontationFail_007=Move the {icon:angrymob_icon} token {_rnd_ConfrontationFail_0} spaces to the left.
ConfrontationFail_008=**ALL players must choose and perform one penalty:**
ConfrontationFail_009=Pay $3.
ConfrontationFail_010=Return 3 resources to the supply.
ConfrontationFail_011=Discard 2 Estate Upgrades.
ConfrontationFail_012=_If this is not possible, they instead_ **lose 5VP**_._

# passages/00195-HunterConf2.mws.yaml
HunterConf2_001=EXPERIMENTS UNLEASHED
HunterConf2_002=All remaining eligible players take all the Experiments they have completed **this Generation** into their hands _(excluding any Masterwork)_. Then, they secretly choose an Experiment card (or no card at all) and keep it hidden under their palm.
HunterConf2_003=Once all players have chosen, all players reveal the card (or no card) they have chosen simultaneously. This card will be discarded after the event is resolved.
HunterConf2_004=Then, players will **count up the total value of the VP on all donated Experiment cards.**
HunterConf2_005=If the value is equal to {huntnum} or higher, the unleashed experiments will succeed.
HunterConf2_006=If the value is less, the hunters will prevail.
HunterConf2_007=Click to start the bid.

# passages/00196-TaxesEventNoConfrontation2.mws.yaml
TaxesEventNoConfrontation2_001=A Pittance
TaxesEventNoConfrontation2_002=While it amounted to little less than political pandering, the Hunters did, however, offer kind words and assurances to the people of {townname} in response to the family's gentle consent to further taxation. This did nothing to soothe the financial stress it placed upon them, nor did it cool their sneering derision when the deeds of the Hunters were brought up in casual conversations about town.
TaxesEventNoConfrontation2_003=All players, in turn order, may choose to either **lose 2** {icon:creepy_icon} or **gain an ingredient** of their choice from the supply.

# passages/00197-GoodNote-Goals_.mws.yaml
GoodNote_Goals__001=Good Goals -
GoodNote_Goals__002=**NOTE: If we do ever add a 5th player, the HUNT on this leg is not coded for 5 players.**
GoodNote_Goals__003=BONUS - Place an End-game goal if one of the Buildings that was Concealed.
GoodNote_Goals__004=Equity - Players that are behind are given a little boost.
GoodNote_Goals__005=Monsters - REAL
GoodNote_Goals__006=Want to spread a message of love and peace to the outside world. They are eco-friendly. They built their own University.
GoodNote_Goals__007=They want us to stop our Experimentations. Maybe we add a Creepy token to our Experiment action.
GoodNote_Goals__008=Maybe we can take an action to be a real swell individual and help out with a mini narrative and lose our Creepy.
GoodNote_Goals__009=Biology Experiments Encouraged
GoodNote_Goals__010=put a storybook token on the Angy Mob token.
GoodNote_Goals__011=Perhaps we should start a FRENZY in town.
GoodNote_Goals__012=Hunters - MONSTERS ARE REAL XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXx
GoodNote_Goals__013=What if we just sent all the Hunters to their valiant deaths. That'd deal with the problem, probably. Right?
GoodNote_Goals__014=1st round, have the option to doubt. VOTE
GoodNote_Goals__015=You are punished as a group for being wrong (Estate Upgrades).
GoodNote_Goals__016=Sponsor Holy relics & weapons. Maybe send someone out into the hills to kill stuff - mini-game.
GoodNote_Goals__017=Give resources and knowledge to win battles. Or let the hero die.
GoodNote_Goals__018=Engineering Experiments encouraged.
GoodNote_Goals__019=Award a different Area of normal Scientific expertise to each player.
GoodNote_Goals__020=Retrieve the **Master's Study** Vanity Estate upgrade tiles.
GoodNote_Goals__022=Starting with the player in Last place and continuing in ascending order by point total, each player chooses a Master's Study tile and adds it to their Estate. No additional cost is paid if a new
GoodNote_Goals__023=<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<Note this.
GoodNote_Goals__024=Monsters come to work for you.
GoodNote_Goals__025=**Choose one of the following options:**
GoodNote_Goals__026=Lose **1VP**, but gain a servant type.
GoodNote_Goals__027=Gain your choice of a **Body** or an **Animal** resource.
GoodNote_Goals__028=Unimplemented Ideas:
GoodNote_Goals__029=If cured. Choose another player. You will eat their Servant.
GoodNote_Goals__030=Any player that had joined the opposite side gains Ingredients equal to the total number of tokens given to players.
GoodNote_Goals__031=Stray line - Even the disfigurements of the lowly caretakers were met with indifference by the local populace.

# passages/00198-PostUniversity-Notes.mws.yaml
PostUniversity_Notes_001=PostUni -
PostUniversity_Notes_002=Mayor is rewarded.
PostUniversity_Notes_003=Charity is rewarded.
PostUniversity_Notes_004=Players are given extra bonus points for being behind. 1st place is considered Creepier, gain 1 Creepy.
PostUniversity_Notes_005=Gameplay changes include a Nobel Prize for the least Creepy scientist.
PostUniversity_Notes_006=1st Gen - Event - Things are TOO GOOD. We need to create the Ultimate Disease.
PostUniversity_Notes_007=If players agree to work towards a master disease, an Ultimate Disease is created. Problem is while a few initial cases are reported, the antibodies this creates essentially give herd immunity to the entire region.
PostUniversity_Notes_008=Immortality thread - players w/ immortality can choose to kill their parent. Sanity reduction.
PostUniversity_Notes_009=Single Card - Ultimate - Anyone can complete it. Once complete:
PostUniversity_Notes_010=2nd Gen - VOTE to unleash the disease or not. Create the Disease or do not.
PostUniversity_Notes_011=Anyone who is behind in Research gains a boost on a track of their choice.

# passages/00199-UniMayor.mws.yaml
UniMayor_001=Legacy of Leadership
UniMayor_002=To christen the advantageous construction of the new university
UniMayor_003=With the continued success of the University
UniMayor_004= and the return of the eccentric family seemingly responsible for that turn of events, the city of {townname} arranged a large parade.
UniMayor_005=Photographs from the event show a disgruntled individual sitting atop a large float made of crocuses and lilies, powered by a newly procured steam and wheel device. {mayor} III does not mention this event within their journal, however it is noted extensively and with great sardonic enthusiasm for the next several months in the journals of their cousins.
UniMayor_006=It was under the leadership of {mayor} that this push for modern sensibilities was first spearheaded and the town could not forget the significance of this event.
UniMayor_007=Retrieve a **Charity Memorial** Estate Tile from the scenario box. {mayor} III may build this in their next available plot. They do not have to pay the cost to open a new plot.
UniMayor_008=Return the Commemorative Mayoral Coin to the scenario box.

# passages/00200-UniCharity.mws.yaml
UniCharity_001=Charity's Legacy
UniCharity_002=It seemed the festivities in {townname} could scarcely cease before another bright and joyous event occurred. Only a few years after a memorial had been erected in the honor of {mayor} III, the Hospital could not contain its admiration as well. {charity} III was offered the same generosity.
UniCharity_003=In honor of {charity}'s legacy of charity, another memorial was revealed at a prestigious ceremony, celebrating the continued medical contributions of {townname}. As a university town, the small village hosted an impressive pedigree of scholars who worked with the most advanced methodology in treatment and disease prevention.
UniCharity_004=It seemed the festivities in {townname} could scarcely cease before another bright and joyous event occurred. Only a few years after a memorial had been erected in the honor of {mayor} III, the Hospital could not contain its admiration as well. It was surprised and overjoyed to discover that the same individual's family was not only responsible for guiding the town politically, but cemented their important legacy of giving.
UniCharity_005={mayor} III was visibly agitated by the intrusion into their affairs, but when offered assistance from top researchers in the region, their surly demeanor softened temporarily. Perhaps the minor inconvenience of friendship and celebration would be worth the boon to their inventions.
UniCharity_006=Retrieve a **Charity Memorial** Estate Tile from the scenario box. {charity} III may build this in their next available plot. They do not have to pay the cost to open a new plot.
UniCharity_007=Immediately move **1 space forward** on the Journal track of your choice _for no cost_. Then, lose **2VP**.

# passages/00201-UniEquity.mws.yaml
UniEquity_001=The Guiding Hand of Science
UniEquity_002=At the behest of the university’s administrators, it was decided to more prominently feature scholarly works produced by local inventors. However, the administration deemed it unwise to promote the works of those who had already solidified their presence in the public eye. The course of action they deemed most appropriate was to provide an “equitable” boost to amplify the standing of lesser-known scientists, to better display the breadth of knowledge and ambition within the humble city of {townname}.
UniEquity_003=The family was disgusted by this “lopsided” display of unmerited assistance. However, they accepted it nonetheless, leaving the most seasoned cousin to grumble at the injustice of it all.

# passages/00202-UniEquity1.mws.yaml
UniEquity1_001=Another Competitive Assessment
UniEquity1_002=The University insisted upon periodic inspections of the laboratories and experimental apparatus being used by interns apportioned from the student body. While each scientist affected a congenial appearance and made sure to conceal their more sinister workings during these assessments, they made no similar attempts to conceal their agitation afterwards.
UniEquity1_003=However, the pitiable honorariums provided to those family members with lesser reputations continued.

# passages/00203-UniEvent1-UltimateDisease.mws.yaml
UniEvent1_UltimateDisease_001=Ignored Amongst the Scientific Elite
UniEvent1_UltimateDisease_002=The {playtxt} cousins watched with dour hearts as the once morose streets were festooned with bright spring colors. Educated middle-class families strolled along the sidewalks in modest clothing. Children laughed and rode bicycles in the park. They shuddered at the sight. It was all **too good**.
UniEvent1_UltimateDisease_003=With the initial festivities over, their estimation had soured in the eyes of the academics. Though they had not been spurned or mistreated, the once generous enthusiasm had waned from repeated ethical infractions, misuse of the medical operating theater, and radical outbursts during local symposiums. And to complicate matters further, it became increasingly obvious that due to the peaceful and progressive values of {townname}, the educated were less troubled with matters of any immediate, existential, or diabolical concern.
UniEvent1_UltimateDisease_004=The solution to this lack of a problem was obvious. If the world refused to create a new, horrific problem to solve, then they would defy nature and create it themselves. Surely, if they combined their efforts, they could create the **ultimate disease**! A disease so infectious that they would forever undo this plague of positivity.
UniEvent1_UltimateDisease_005=This would certainly **rid them of this unfair and blatant balancing** of fortunes.

# passages/00204-UniEvent2-UltimateDisease.mws.yaml
UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_001=The Ultimate Disease
UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_002=As the oppressive sunshine illuminated the study of 
UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_003={_rnd_UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_4} 
UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_004={_rnd_UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_0} 
UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_005={_rnd_UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_1} 
UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_006={_rnd_UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_2} 
UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_007={_rnd_UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_3} 
UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_008=III, the cousins assembled to finalize their creation. With a large piece of parchment sprawled across the desk and delightful bean strudels with heavy cream for refreshment, the scientists began to formulate a blueprint using the knowledge they had gained from recent experimentations.
UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_009=Some, however, were more forthcoming with information than others.
UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_010=Players will now vote to collaborate with their knowledge to create a new disease. All players take their Voting token into their hand. Players will secretly choose a side to place face up in their palm. Then, they will close their fist and extend it to the center of the table.
UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_011=A **Yay** vote is a vote to discard **1 completed Chemistry or Occult Experiment**.
UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_012=A **Nay** vote is a vote to NOT contribute an experiment.
UniEvent2_UltimateDisease_013=When all players have chosen, all players reveal their vote. Tally all votes and the side with the most votes wins. _Ties are considered a win for the "yay" vote._

# passages/00205-UniEvent2-Success.mws.yaml
UniEvent2_Success_001=A Wondrous Success
UniEvent2_Success_002=Symptoms: Nausea, fever, vomiting, hypertension, drowsiness, loss of libido, skin lesions, blurred vision, heart palpitations, headache, weight-loss, chronic pain, demonic possession. The prospectus for the ultimate disease included nearly every side-effect known to science. The cousins spent the late-night hours laughing till their throats were hoarse as they concocted the elixir.
UniEvent2_Success_003=The following week, the disease was released at the Farmer's Market, a tincture of the foul liquid smashed against the steps. It proved communicable within seconds and the noxious gases spread from person-to-person with each dry cough.
UniEvent2_Success_004=However, the effect was not altogether anticipated. This grim amalgamation of deadly diseases, while invoking minor symptoms in some initially exposed, caused antibodies to build up within the region, nullifying their effects and strengthening their systems against infection. By creating a disease that included all known symptoms, they had essentially inoculated the populace against all disease simultaneously.
UniEvent2_Success_005=It wasn't long before the university traced the source of the marvel to the cousins. Word soon traveled about their research, and the town applauded yet another triumph for science and the world! Clearly, this family of scientists needed no assistance in their heavenly endeavors.
UniEvent2_Success_006=Any player that voted to contribute discards a **completed** Chemistry or Occult Experiment. Each player that contributed **gains 2 resources** of their choice from the supply.
UniEvent2_Success_007=Any player that did not contribute **gains 1** {icon:creepy_icon}**.**

# passages/00206-UniEvent2-Failure.mws.yaml
UniEvent2_Failure_001=Unfortunate Failure
UniEvent2_Failure_002=With the cousins guarding their knowledge and no consensus on how to move forward, the meeting soon devolved into bickering and one-upmanship. Each cousin pontificated at length their personal achievements and the unexpressed envy the others had towards their work. Many of the pastries were left half-eaten that night.
UniEvent2_Failure_003=As the science was unsuccessful, they each retired to their estates in the late evening to let the familial jibes fester in their minds.
UniEvent2_Failure_004=The town remained unaffected by their exchange of harsh words. And as before, they continued to offer assistance to those who they felt were lacking the resources. What a pitiable learning opportunity.
UniEvent2_Failure_005=Each player counts the total amount of levels they have gained on their Journal Research Tracks. The player with the lowest total **moves their research marker forward 1 level** on the track of their choice at no cost. _If there is a tie, ties are broken by the player with the least VP._
UniEvent2_Failure_006=Each player counts the total amount of levels they have gained on their Journal Research Tracks. The **2** players with the lowest total **move their research marker forward 1 level** on the track of their choice at no cost. _If there is a tie, ties are broken by the player with the least VP._
UniEvent2_Failure_007=Any player that voted "yay" to contribute does not discard an Experiment. But, they **lose 1** {icon:creepy_icon}.

# passages/00207-CharityAwardGood.mws.yaml
CharityAwardGood_002=**Consideration of Righteousness**
CharityAwardGood_003=The Fraternity was correct to be cautious in their dealings with the eccentric family whose ominous visitings within the city carried a sinister air about them. However, their fears could not completely overshadow their righteous convictions.
CharityAwardGood_004={charity} III's familial legacy of **charity** was instrumental in sharing the gift of knowledge. Modern weaponry had transformed the Hunter's ability to fight against the evil forces threatening to overtake the city. And it was this malignant sentiment that forced their hand to offer a token of their appreciation.
CharityAwardGood_005=Retrieve the **Personal Library** Estate Upgrade from the scenario box. You may immediately build it in the next empty plot on your Estate board at no additional cost. Then, return the Heart{icon:s1_hearttoken}token to the scenario box.

# passages/00208-MayoralAward.mws.yaml
MayoralAward_002=**The Benefit of Knowledge**
MayoralAward_003=The path to enlightenment is a not without its humble beginnings, and the creatures that now embraced a gentler path could not have done so without an intense pursuit of knowledge. The deviant machinations of a cruel world may have doomed them to these egregious forms, but to find peace with one's self is a struggle all beings face.
MayoralAward_004=The townsfolk appreciated {mayor} III's lineage as partly responsible for spearheading the gift of **knowledge** above all else in the generations past. They desire to repay this Librarian lineage with a contribution of their own.
MayoralAward_005=Retrieve the **Personal Library** Estate Upgrade from the scenario box. You may immediately build it in the next empty plot on your Estate board at no additional cost. Then, return the **Commemorative Mayoral Coin** to the box.
MayoralAward_006=Whenever you take the Perform Experiment action, the **Personal Library** provides one free Knowledge of your choice from the supply. This Knowledge can be used immediately towards the cost of Performing that Experiment.

# passages/00209-HunterJoin.mws.yaml
HunterJoin_001=A messenger arrives at sunset wearing a pendant around their neck with a golden bow and arrow insignia upon it. They wait expectantly for your correspondence.
HunterJoin_002=Pledge your service to the Fraternity of Hunters.

# passages/00210-RefusalEvent.mws.yaml
RefusalEvent_001=An Illuminating Conversation
RefusalEvent_002=As the black carriage approached, the young man paused in his duties and lit a small pipe. In these dark times, a stablehand knew more about the comings and goings of the townsfolk than most anyone in the region. A few conspiratorial words and he was generous with information.
RefusalEvent_003=**I introduced myself as:**

# passages/00211-JoinedAlready.mws.yaml
JoinedAlready_001=A Busy Day
JoinedAlready_002=The man looked at {meet} quizzically for a moment before shaking his head and returning to work. {meet} had already joined a faction and continued on their way after the fog cleared from their mind.

# passages/00212-EquitableValues.mws.yaml
EquitableValues_001=Deplorable Equity
EquitableValues_002=For the first time in decades, the townsfolk expressed a sense of community, a singular and modern identity. 
EquitableValues_003=While members of the Fraternity attended to their dark business, sharpening their skills and weapons on their own, the town remained resolute in their ability to rid the surrounding hills of evil.
EquitableValues_004=The Order of St. Hubertus remained an official moniker, but a new, more democratic society emerged. The secrets that had remained hidden for so long had finally been exposed and the sense of freedom was finally something worth protecting.
EquitableValues_005=Unlike previous generations that were keen to allow an aloof eccentric to isolate themselves amongst the rocky crags at the valley's edge, the townsfolk became determined in their attempts to ingratiate the obstinate cousins into the fold. While the reception was always cold and the iron gates and foreboding wooden doorways were mostly closed to them, they never stopped trying.
EquitableValues_006=While they would never admit to it, the ones who were most desperate tended to accept the offers more readily.
EquitableValues_007=The player with the fewest VP gains 1 of their Servants from Lost. _Ties are broken by the player who went last in the previous round._
EquitableValues_008=The **2** players with the fewest VP gain 1 of their Servants from Lost. _Ties are broken by the player who went last in the previous round._
EquitableValues_009=The player with the most points gains 2 {icon:creepy_icon}.

# passages/00213-LycanMessageGood.mws.yaml
LycanMessageGood_001=**The Form of the Wolf**
LycanMessageGood_002=Though the sight had now become commonplace, confirming the existence of persons with the ability to change into an animal form had remarkable consequences. It is possible that it even disrupted the studies of one of our kin.

# passages/00214-WolvesEco-Friendly.mws.yaml
WolvesEco_Friendly_001=A Message
WolvesEco_Friendly_002=As the new decade began, the motley parade of beastly horrors had turned their claws from weapons of destruction into instruments of cultivation. They embraced modern amenities and fashions, walking the streets with upright strides as the town continued to thrive.
WolvesEco_Friendly_003=For most, however, this new sense of peace was tarnished by the persistence of past injustices. As newspaper pressings became even more accessible, pamphlets and signage began to circulate amongst the populace.
WolvesEco_Friendly_004="Our brethren; abused, slaughtered, and experimented upon. No more! We can bear this injustice no longer." One paper stated, "Meat is murder."
WolvesEco_Friendly_005=Most had adopted a Pythagorean diet, developing a keen culinary taste for vegetable curries and rich, barley porridge. While it was not strictly forbidden to consume the cooked flesh of domestic animals, when the cousins' town business included a stop by the Farmer's Market, the townsfolk looked away in horror, mothers shielding their furred children's eyes as the implication was too much for them to bear.
WolvesEco_Friendly_006=Yet still roiling beneath the thin veneer of prim etiquette, a baser nature threatened to reemerge anew.
WolvesEco_Friendly_007=Put a {icon:creepy_icon} token on the **Farmer's Market**.

# passages/00215-AngryMobStorybook.mws.yaml
AngryMobStorybook_001=A Frightful Day
AngryMobStorybook_002=To be awakened early morning after a late night's work was agitating, but to awake to a shrill, blood-curdling scream was something else entirely.
AngryMobStorybook_003=A woman in a modest blue dress crouched near the entrance to the estate, her blood-covered maw held within two clawed hands as she wailed in distress. A few feet away, two wolves clad in sharp business suits huddled over the dead body of a servant, tearing into the flesh with their teeth and claws as fresh blood flowed down the gravel drive.
AngryMobStorybook_004=A monster stood nearby, clearly resisting the urge to join into the fray. He fixed his tie and wiped away saliva from his chin before speaking in a solemn voice. "Poor thing couldn't control herself. Took the first bite. Terrible tragedy. Awfully sorry."
AngryMobStorybook_005=Perhaps it was unavoidable that the close proximity of humanity to the beasts would incite such an event.
AngryMobStorybook_006=There were moments when the rage amongst the townsfolk would well up and explode in uncontrollably violent outbursts. For the monsters of {townname}, these were no longer represented by torches or pitchforks held high, but by a feverish bloodlust.
AngryMobStorybook_007=As such, it was a calm Sunday afternoon when a local werewolf doffed his cap and interrupted tea time by holding up a blood-stained and torn piece of fabric.
AngryMobStorybook_008=He placed the scrap onto the table. "We would return the body to you for proper burial if it were still possible," he shrugged, his ears flattening. "But, you know how it goes when bones are involved. Sorry."
AngryMobStorybook_009=Another good servant gone. It was somewhat inevitable, yet still an unfortunate loss of life, time and money.
AngryMobStorybook_010=Return a Servant to Lost. 
AngryMobStorybook_011=Then lose **{_rnd_AngryMobStorybook_0}VP**.
AngryMobStorybook_012=Move your {icon:creepy_icon} token **2 spaces** to the left. Move the {icon:angrymob_icon} token **3 spaces** to the right _(or as far as possible)_.

# passages/00216-GoodFrenzyEvent.mws.yaml
GoodFrenzyEvent_001=A Reasoned Proposal
GoodFrenzyEvent_002=While the system of progressive monster reform was altruistic, it was not without its imperfections. Infractions ranging from minor maulings to severe interdental jugular removal were noted over the years, as were the manic episodes associated with these incidents.
GoodFrenzyEvent_003=It was clear that humans were marginally upset about the lack of livestock and uptick in missing persons potentially consumed by wolves. It was also clear that each monster would experience near daily urges to indulge in profane behavior that they were forced to suppress.
GoodFrenzyEvent_004=Perhaps, they suggested, if they could attempt to indulge their darker urges in a safe space where this expression was fully encouraged, then it would pacify those urges at other more domestic times.

# passages/00217-YesFrenzy.mws.yaml
YesFrenzy_001=The FRENZY
YesFrenzy_002=The townsfolk who chose not to participate locked their doors and boarded their windows, but the first howls of ghoulish delight sent those same individuals clawing at the walls to be released into the wild again. The Frenzy spared no person in {townname}. The unhinged spectacle set the teeth gnashing and a passionate fire blazing both metaphorically and physically, plumes of hot embers erupting upwards from homes set ablaze with wild abandon. When a door burst open or a window shattered, barely a strangled cry could be heard before another victim's fresh blood spilled into the streets.
YesFrenzy_003=Indulging in latent urges proved not to quell the dormant urges of the citizenry, but to stoke it. In the coming weeks, the logical faculties of the changed townfolk were removed. And in its place, a well of anger and a bloodlust so acute it left the landscape to darken and the soil to sour!
YesFrenzy_004=The thin line between civility and savagery had been severed. The monsters were set loose to prowl the region and invoke their hideous reign upon the unsuspecting masses.

# passages/00218-NoFrenzy.mws.yaml
NoFrenzy_001=A Reasoned Response
NoFrenzy_002=The recommendation was accepted with gravitas. While many remained wistful, the group's almost immediate adoption of the concept made it clearly a dangerous proposition.
NoFrenzy_003=To further preoccupy their minds and to quell the bloodlust just beneath the surface, they offered further building assistance to reinforce a wider variety of scientific disciplines.
NoFrenzy_004=Retrieve the **Chemistry** and **Engineering Master's Study** Vanity Estate Upgrades from the scenario box and place them nearby. Any time you gain a Vanity Estate Upgrade, you may choose to gain 1 of these instead.

# passages/00219-WolvesEvil2.mws.yaml
WolvesEvil2_001=Once More the Accursed Contribution
WolvesEvil2_002=The messenger did not appear until nightfall, whereupon the lateness of arrival interrupted the cousins' dessert and coffee. The moonlight reflected off his steel gaze as he entered the sitting room without invitation. His fangs had tasted blood that same night.
WolvesEvil2_003=The family could delay their offering no longer and the beasts of the Order salivated with anticipation over the knowledge they would soon acquire.
WolvesEvil2_004=If a player donates, they will receive an immediate bonus based on the level of Experiment they donate (_higher levels granting higher rewards_).

# passages/00220-TCOD-TownName.mws.yaml
TCOD_TownName_001=The Village
TCOD_TownName_002=Now that our given names have been established, we must also search our recollection for the name of the village which our vast estates overlook. Considering the myriad of small towns in the Hungarian countryside, it would be unmeritably forward to not allow the group a chance to collectively name the place they will now inhabit.
TCOD_TownName_003=Click here to name the village...

# passages/00221-NameEntryTownConfirm.mws.yaml
NameEntryTownConfirm_001=Thank you and please do excuse our forgetfulness.
NameEntryTownConfirm_002=Of course, {townname} is an appropriate and fitting moniker for a place to conduct important scientific research. In fact, history will remember this name, mark my words.

# passages/00222-Preparations-TCOD.mws.yaml
Preparations_TCOD_001=Preparations
Preparations_TCOD_002=Complete the standard setup for {playtxt} players as shown in the rulebook. _Note that the_ {icon:angrymob_icon} _track and starting player will be set by the Storybook in the coming pages._
Preparations_TCOD_003=Then, retrieve **The Cost of Disease** Scenario box, which will contain all components needed for this story. As the Storybook progresses, it will ask you to put items into play from this box. Be sure to keep it nearby.

# passages/00223-Preface-TCOD.mws.yaml
Preface_TCOD_001=A Foreword
Preface_TCOD_002=Herein contains a historical account of a peculiar lineage. One that spans multiple generations and by all accounts will continue to fascinate historians for many years to come.
Preface_TCOD_003=I have endeavored to provide as complete a scholarly history as one could provide given the conflicting accounts and whims of hearsay. While many of the details, haunting to the imagination as they may be, stretch the very limits of our human understanding, it is my hope that this text and the accompanying research materials procured will provide evidence as to their truth. The harrowing and potentially supernatural series of events has the capacity to shake the very foundations of the scientific world as we perceive it.
Preface_TCOD_004=With deference to the fellowship that commissioned this explicit work, though I have never met with these generous benefactors, I humbly submit this biographical account in its entirety and swear by the veracity of the contents within.
Preface_TCOD_005=In good health,
Preface_TCOD_006=Dr. Ensign Benwallis

# passages/00224-ImmortalitySetup.mws.yaml
ImmortalitySetup_001=**To Infinity**

# passages/00225-Diseases2.mws.yaml
Diseases2_001=**Wasted Potential**
Diseases2_002=While the disease that plagued the scientists was manageable, the effects were still tiresome. Time spent advancing what they considered "true science" was instead squandered upon practical medical applications to assuage their own afflictions.
Diseases2_003=All players that have not completed their **Hereditary Disease Experiment** must **lose 2VP**.
Diseases2_004=**A Cleansing**
Diseases2_005=When the symptoms grew too fierce, they locked themselves away inside one of the myriad rooms of their estate. This resulted in an unfortunate loss of productivity and an odiferous contamination. When chemicals would not suffice for cleansing, it was deemed necessary to burn the entire room and start again.
Diseases2_006=All players that have not completed their **Hereditary Disease Experiment** must **discard an Estate Upgrade tile** to the box or **lose 3VP**.

# passages/00226-DiseaseEnd.mws.yaml
DiseaseEnd_001=Longevity and Clarity
DiseaseEnd_002=Notes from this time period detail potential blueprints for a special room; a sanguine coagulant encased in a glass bubble and fed with an electrical current. Although there are no further mentions of the device, peculiarities in historical accounts suggest that some in the next generation received advice and assistance from an unknown source.
DiseaseEnd_003=Click here to determine the fate of the town...
DiseaseEnd_004=Retrieve the **Stasis Chamber Estate Upgrade tiles** from the Scenario box. Any player with a completed, face-down, **Hereditary Disease Experiment** has the option of building the Stasis Chamber in their Estate. Players with the Hereditary Disease Experiment **stored** cannot accept this bonus. _You must still pay $ if you would like to build this tile in a new plot, or you can replace an existing Estate tile._
DiseaseEnd_005=Then, discard any face-down Hereditary Disease cards to the scenario box, along with any remaining Stasis Chamber Estate Upgrades.

# passages/00227-WolfJoin.mws.yaml
WolfJoin_001=A messenger in a gray cloak marked with the insignia of a wolf's head arrived at the estate one evening. They smiled and the gleam of their white teeth shone in the moonlight.
WolfJoin_002=Pledge your service to the Order of St. Hubertus.

# passages/00228-HelpingEvil.mws.yaml
HelpingEvil_001=A Reward for Service
HelpingEvil_002=Upon receipt of their inheritance, the newest Generation of scientists were surprised to find a generous addendum attached by the {society}. Aside from the notoriety afforded by this gift, as promised, a permanent structure was to be erected on their properties to aid in their experimental pursuits.
HelpingEvil_003=Retrieve the **{society}** tokens. Retrieve the **Master's Study** Vanity Estate Upgrades.
HelpingEvil_004={nameA} III gains **4VP** and gains a {society} token.
HelpingEvil_005={nameB} III gains **4VP** and gains a {society} token.
HelpingEvil_006={nameC} III gains **4VP** and gains a {society} token.
HelpingEvil_007={nameD} III gains **4VP** and gains a {society} token.
HelpingEvil_008={nameE} III gains **4VP** and gains a {society} token.

# passages/00229-MWTokenResolve.mws.yaml
MWTokenResolve_001=The Work is Complete
MWTokenResolve_002=The gathering of clawed monstrosities celebrated with keening wails as the Masterwork was completed in all of its glory. Surely, the legacy of the family would be secured forever. Yet, the watchful, glowing eyes of the crowd did not share this same deference to sentimentality.
MWTokenResolve_003=A furious cacophony of growls sounded as the monsters surrounded the experiment. Some scribbled away at notes, copying the formulas and schematics as best as they could while others simply traced every minute detail with their fingers and observed with interest.
MWTokenResolve_004=It was clear that they would have been much more able to understand and reproduce the results of the experiment if they had been given earlier access to the cousin's work over the years.
MWTokenResolve_005=Resolve your Masterwork as normal. Then, for each Experiment under your Masterwork, **lose 4VP**. Discard all cards under your Masterwork.

# passages/00230-Evilsforgive.mws.yaml
Evilsforgive_001=**Still Wary**
Evilsforgive_002=For the family members that had aided them in their efforts, they wore wide false-smiles and offered toasts to their continued partnership. But, for those who had plotted against them, they remained wary.
Evilsforgive_003={nameA} III **immediately gains 1** {icon:creepy_icon}.
Evilsforgive_004={nameB} III **immediately gains 1** {icon:creepy_icon}.
Evilsforgive_005={nameC} III **immediately gains 1** {icon:creepy_icon}.
Evilsforgive_006={nameD} III **immediately gains 1** {icon:creepy_icon}.
Evilsforgive_007={nameE} III **immediately gains 1** {icon:creepy_icon}.
Evilsforgive_008=**Forgiveness**
Evilsforgive_009=The scientists' doubts were put at ease when a werewolf in a brown sack suit took to the podium to preside over a town meeting. A mixture of lycanthropic beings, horned beasts, and those still holding onto their humanity were in attendance outside the school. The force of the wolf's words caused tears to stream down their cheeks.
Evilsforgive_010="We want to shatter those unfortunate stereotypes. We hold no grudges. We want to work with you all, not against you. The child should not be punished for the sins of the father. You are all welcome." The werewolf blew their cold nose into their handkerchief as a rumbling cheer rose from the crowd.
Evilsforgive_011=As a token of this myth-shattering event, many handshakes were exchanged that day and a promise was made to press forward into a more modern era; an era where science could improve their lives ten-fold!
Evilsforgive_012=Retrieve the **Master's Study** Vanity Estate Upgrade tiles.
Evilsforgive_013=Starting with the player in last place and continuing in ascending order by point total, each player chooses a **Master's Study** tile and adds it to their Estate. No additional cost is paid for a new plot to place this tile. _(Ties are broken by the player that went later in turn order in the previous round.)_

# passages/00231-SymposiumMiddle.mws.yaml
SymposiumMiddle_001=A Cure for Yellow Fever
SymposiumMiddle_002="Vague, tawdry." The notes from the lectures created a tableau of mixed reactions. 
SymposiumMiddle_003="Delightfully crude, but potentially insightful. Overall though, the lectures were amusing for what they lacked in substance."
SymposiumMiddle_004="All angst and ambition without respect for traditional ethics or the scientific method. Unsupported hypotheses, and rapid-fire homeopathic conjecture."
SymposiumMiddle_005="Of note, however, was one intriguing if not juvenile statement. I jotted the quote down for posterity and so that others at the state may enjoy it when I plaster the message all across the lavatories. The quote:
SymposiumMiddle_006='It's simple. Wash your hands after you touch your butt.'"
SymposiumMiddle_007=At first they seemed intrigued, but the presentations, while exciting, proved to have only minimal scientific value in their eyes. It was decided by the majority to research any other notable discoveries in their portfolio before making their recommendations.
SymposiumMiddle_008=And without the publication of a proposed **Yellow Fever** inoculation, their decision on the value of a university in a small town in Hungary was easy to make.
SymposiumMiddle_009=And it was the **publication** of a **Yellow Fever** inoculation from an otherwise unknown town in Hungary that made their decision to build a University in the region much easier.

# passages/00232-PanaceaUnleashCons1.mws.yaml
PanaceaUnleashCons1_002=With the passing of the generation, the hideous and well-founded rumors regarding the grisly demise and otherwise negative treatment of servants in the family's households faded into history. As considerably misguided as it was, the allure of steady employ once again attracted new applicants to the estates once more.
PanaceaUnleashCons1_003=Any players with a Servant in the game box retrieves it from the box and adds it to Lost.

# passages/00233-PanaceaUnleashCons2.mws.yaml
PanaceaUnleashCons2_001=With the passing of the generation, the hideous and well-founded rumors regarding the grisly demise and otherwise negative treatment of servants within the family's households faded into history. As considerably misguided as it would have been, the allure of steady employ once again attracted new applicants to their estates.
PanaceaUnleashCons2_002=Any players with a Servant in the game box may retrieve it from the box and place it in Lost.

# passages/00234-TipsnTricks.mws.yaml
TipsnTricks_001=It is almost never advantageous for all players to take the same route.
TipsnTricks_002=All decisions carry with them consequences, both good and bad. 

# passages/00235-NoHospitalCons.mws.yaml
NoHospitalCons_001=A Steady Focus
NoHospitalCons_002=For members of this ignoble family, it was not uncommon for personal labors to consume an individual's waking thoughts and cause them to forget even the most simplistic of instructions. But for those that toiled endlessly on their infernal schemes, their reward - aside from obesity and appalling hygiene - was one of a deeper understanding.
NoHospitalCons_003=**Dr. {nameA} III**
NoHospitalCons_004=Move forward **1 level on the Journal Track of your choice**.
NoHospitalCons_005=**Dr. {nameB} III**
NoHospitalCons_006=**Dr. {nameC} III**
NoHospitalCons_007=**Dr. {nameD} III**
NoHospitalCons_008=**Dr. {nameE} III**

# passages/00236-S5HospA3.mws.yaml
S5HospA3_001=**The Allure of Discovery**
S5HospA3_002=While the Panacea proposed may not have approached the problem in an ethical nor fiscally responsible way, the simple gesture garnered much attention from the academic community. Along with the famed discovery of a "cure" for Yellow Fever, this potential for scientific advancement was too strong to ignore.
S5HospA3_003=The family soon found a rapt audience for their unconventional experimentations, despite all logic running counter to this development, and the city entered into a golden age of progress.
S5HospA3_004=**Relentless Opposition**
S5HospA3_005=The church's distrust of science has riled up the populace. Contributions to the Hospital's original construction notwithstanding, without the hope provided by a **Panacea** to remove ailments en masse, the townsfolk became determined to return to the old ways.
S5HospA3_006=A most pitiful display that led to stagnation and the return of the pestilence that once was eliminated from the land.
S5HospA3_007=The church's distrust of science has riled up the populace. Contributions to the Hospital's original construction notwithstanding, the nonsensical decision to **unleash** the proposed Panacea resulted in a loss of the original formula. Without the hope provided by a **Panacea** to remove ailments en masse, the townsfolk became determined to return to the old ways.

# passages/00237-NewMaster3E.mws.yaml
NewMaster3E_001=**The {_rnd_NewMaster3E_0} {creationE}**

# passages/00238-MWCreationHubE.mws.yaml
MWCreationHubE_001=**{creationE}**
MWCreationHubE_002=1 Body, 1 {cost2E}, 3 Occult, 3 {costE}
MWCreationHubE_003=2 Animals, 5 Biology, 1 {costE}
MWCreationHubE_004=1 Animal, 1 {cost2E}, 3 Biology, 3 {costE}
MWCreationHubE_005=2 Gears, 5 Engineering, 1 {costE}
MWCreationHubE_006=1 Gear, 1 {cost2E}, 4 Engineering, 2 {costE}
MWCreationHubE_007=2 Chemicals, 4 Chemistry, 2 {costE}
MWCreationHubE_008=1 Bottle, 1 {cost2E}, 3 Chemistry, 3 {costE}
MWCreationHubE_009=2 Bodies, 4 Occult, 1 {costE}

# passages/00239-MWCompleteHubE.mws.yaml
MWCompleteHubE_001=**{_rnd_MWCompleteHubE_0} - {nameE} - Journal Entry Excerpt**
MWCompleteHubE_002=The preparations proved tedious, but the resulting wave of spiritual energy as the ritual was completed left me standing in awe of my creation. The {creationE} was a brilliant success. And the powers I now harnessed were unthinkable!
MWCompleteHubE_003=To see my work in the flesh, to see {creationE} finally realized; the passion of the moment overwhelmed my senses. I had done it. I shook my fist at God and all who doubted me! You were wrong! I am invincible!
MWCompleteHubE_004=A brief, blinding flash and the work was done. I threw my goggles to the floor to gaze upon my creation with my own eyes - {creationE}. The polished metal surface whirred with interior mechanisms churning - then, glorious motion! Oh wondrous automaton, with you by my side the scientific world will be humbled!
MWCompleteHubE_005=I tapped the glass bottle, watching the liquid inside swirl and glow with the purity of the mixture. The {creationE} had been a stunning success and once mass production could be attained, my family's legacy would be secure. I laughed. Then, laughed again. My cacophonous laughter echoed off the stone walls of my estate for years to come.
MWCompleteHubE_006=I observed the effects as the syringe filled with {creationE} emptied its contents into the unwilling test subject. Just as I had expected, the reaction was immediate and effusive. For so many years, I had toiled away in the solitude of my estate, and now as I wiped the tears from eyes, my beautiful creation was finally complete.
MWCompleteHubE_007=The world darkened around me as the {creationE} emerged from a void-like rift in time and space. I could feel the immense power of the insidious being, the air hot with the energy of their presence. They turned to me and with a deep growl, they stated, "Master." I had done it. I was now in control and the world would rue the day they doubted {nameE} III!

# passages/00240-CureNegCons.mws.yaml
CureNegCons_001=Distrust in Medicine
CureNegCons_002=With the Hospital slowly falling into disrepair, the church took great measures to warn the populace of the dangers of inoculation, espousing the virtues of alternative homeopathic remedies and pious living. Inevitably, this led to clusters of Yellow Fever once again appearing within the region.
CureNegCons_003=Having no target for their anger, in a befuddled daze, they turned against the scientist responsible for introducing the cure, without whom this self-inflicted moral dilemma would never have existed.
CureNegCons_004=**Move the** {icon:angrymob_icon} **token 1 space to the left.** {fevercure} immediately **gains 1** {icon:creepy_icon} and **gains 1** {icon:insanity_icon}.

# passages/00241-YellowFeverCureSignin.mws.yaml
YellowFeverCureSignin_001=Yellow Fever Inoculation
YellowFeverCureSignin_002=Through sheer perseverance and months of exposing both themselves, their spouse, all their servants, and several delivery persons to potential curing agents in different hues of yellow, a surprisingly effective solution was created that could be administered intravenously.
YellowFeverCureSignin_003=**Which individual completed the Yellow Fever Inoculation Experiment?**

