# passages/00332-END-HuntersEvil2.mws.yaml
END_HuntersEvil2_001=Overshadowed and Exploited
END_HuntersEvil2_002=While this history may contain a modicum of inconceivable occurrences that stretch the limits of the imagination, it remains a peculiar story relegated to an obscure place and time. It is a mostly forgotten artifact of an era of pseudo-science and speculation that amounted to very little historical significance.
END_HuntersEvil2_003=For it was not the experimentations of {playtxt} ambitious and incredulous scientists that were remembered, it was the Hunters that amassed fame, wealth, and respect on the backs of the superstitious peasants. The disease that wreaked havoc on the countryside was ignored; recast as a demonic presence from folklore; one that could only be kept at bay through the continued vigilance of the Fraternity of Hunters, which of course came at a great financial cost.
END_HuntersEvil2_004=Over the next several years, the Fraternity and its members abandoned the town for more lucrative positions within the government. Soon the not-so-secret society became the affluent aristocrats controlling the entirety of the Hungarian political establishment from the shadows. And the family, who once commanded a measure of reverence, were assigned to obscure prefectures of their own across the country.
END_HuntersEvil2_005=If this story is to be believed, then their knowledge still remains trapped within the decaying walls of stone estates overlooking the forgotten village of {townname}. The work was finally over.

# passages/00333-END-WolvesEvil2.mws.yaml
END_WolvesEvil2_001=The Spread of Evil
END_WolvesEvil2_002=I write these final words under candle-light, from a shelter I have fashioned in the crawl-space beneath the manor. For a desk, a dusty plank of cedar. I try to keep my utensils above the floor which can become musty and dank during my frequent overnight stays: a dull quill, ink, several lengths of charcoal, a ream of parchment. It is no longer safe to sleep in my bed when night falls. The creatures emerge from the shadows to feed on the few souls that still remain, or to irreversibly change them into shambling horrors most unimaginable.
END_WolvesEvil2_003=To think that my work to uncover the genealogy of a mildly successful scientific family would cause me to become consumed by a maelstrom of spreading evil! It is my hope that when I complete this writing (if I complete this writing), that these words will offer a history to condemn these fools and their complicity with demons. The world must know who is responsible. It must condemn the group who coddled darkness and made a mockery of science!
END_WolvesEvil2_004=O God, I hear the creatures again! Their malformed claw-tips scratching at the floorboards! Damn them for what they have done! Damn this infernal work. For it has unleashed a plague upon the land of which there can be no end in sight.

# passages/00334-2p-FrenzyALT.mws.yaml
_2p_FrenzyALT_001=Frenzy Decision
_2p_FrenzyALT_004=**BID**
_2p_FrenzyALT_005=All players take all of their money into their hands. They then secretly choose any amount to place into their right hand to bid on choosing the outcome.
_2p_FrenzyALT_006=**Encouraging** the Frenzy will guarantee that experimentation will no longer be considered Creepy, but also introduces other problems.
_2p_FrenzyALT_007=**Not encouraging** the Frenzy will maintain the Biology award.
_2p_FrenzyALT_008=Once all players are ready, reveal the amount of money bid simultaneously. The player that bid the most wins the vote and also **gains 2VP**. _(If there is a tie, the player who went last in turn order the previous round wins the bid.)_

# passages/00335-GoodFrenzyEvent2.mws.yaml
GoodFrenzyEvent2_001=A Frenzied Decision
GoodFrenzyEvent2_002=All players take their Voting tokens into their hands. The players will secretly choose a side to place face up in their palm. Then they will close their fist and extend it to the center of the table.
GoodFrenzyEvent2_003=A **Yay** vote is a vote to encourage the Frenzy. _This will guarantee that experimentation will no longer be considered Creepy, but creates other problems._
GoodFrenzyEvent2_004=A **Nay** vote is a vote to **not** encourage the Frenzy. _This will maintain the Biology award._

# passages/00336-2p-S5SpecialVoteALT.mws.yaml
_2p_S5SpecialVoteALT_001=BID
_2p_S5SpecialVoteALT_002=All players take all of their money into their hands. They then secretly choose any amount to place in their right hand to bid on choosing the outcome.
_2p_S5SpecialVoteALT_003=The winning player will **gain 3VP** and have the option to choose if the town gains or rejects electricity. Once all players are ready, reveal the amount of money bid simultaneously. _(If there is a tie, the player who went last in turn order the previous round wins the bid.)_
_2p_S5SpecialVoteALT_004=Accepting electricity which will **allow us to complete experiments at a discounted cost** despite the fact that it may enrage the populace into **destruction of property**.
_2p_S5SpecialVoteALT_005=Rejecting electricity will support the obstinate masses and **quell the Angry Mob**.
_2p_S5SpecialVoteALT_006=Once all players are ready, reveal the amount of money bid simultaneously. The player that bid the most wins the ability to choose.
_2p_S5SpecialVoteALT_007=Only the player that wins the bid must pay their bid to the supply.

# passages/00337-WinnerHUBproblem.mws.yaml
WinnerHUBproblem_001=What I'm trying to do is compare all the entered scores and find the winner. BUT, this code below doesn't take into account TIES.
WinnerHUBproblem_002=FIRST TIE-BREAKER:
WinnerHUBproblem_003=Did all tied players complete their Masterwork?
WinnerHUBproblem_004=YES.
WinnerHUBproblem_005=NO.
WinnerHUBproblem_006=If no, choose the tied players that COMPLETED their Masterwork.
WinnerHUBproblem_007=(display tied player names with a multiple-checkable boxes beside them)
WinnerHUBproblem_008=SECOND TIE-BREAKER:
WinnerHUBproblem_009=Which tied player built the most Estate Upgrades?
WinnerHUBproblem_010=(display tied players' names with a single checkable box beside them)
WinnerHUBproblem_011=(also display checkable box that says "Still tied")
WinnerHUBproblem_012=If **still tied**, set the {winner} to "the family."
WinnerHUBproblem_013=Otherwise, set {winner} to the winner.

# passages/00339-AltStartPreviews.mws.yaml
AltStartPreviews_001=Welcome to
AltStartPreviews_002=**MY FATHER'S WORK**
AltStartPreviews_003=Preview Edition
AltStartPreviews_004=This is a preview prototype version of the full My Father's Work game and includes the complete scenario: **The Cost of Disease**. This version only includes the **text** needed to play which should be read aloud to all players when appropriate.
AltStartPreviews_005=The final version will be available as a free download for Apple and Android devices. It will feature gorgeous illustrations, atmospheric audio, helpful visual examples, introductory voice narration, and additional modes to track player scores and unlocked Endings. For the moment, we ask your patience as we labor to bring the full digital version into existence.

