# passages/00353-MayorResolveHunters.mws.yaml
MayorResolveHunters_001=Recompense for Past Leadership
MayorResolveHunters_002=Though memories of the past may be harsh or serene, one cannot deny the significance of those distinctive few whose actions set the gears in motion. {mayor}'s namesake was still whispered amongst the townfolk of {townname}. {mayor}'s contribution to the wellbeing of all may have been acute, but it was noticeable nonetheless.
MayorResolveHunters_003={mayor}'s family legacy, whether through infamy or prestige, raged onward to press upon the boundaries of science and common decency.
MayorResolveHunters_004={mayor} gains **{_rnd_MayorResolveHunters_0}VP**. Gain 1 {icon:creepy_icon}.
MayorResolveHunters_005=Return the **Commemorative Mayoral Coin** to the scenario box.

# passages/00354-ResolveCharityWolves.mws.yaml
ResolveCharityWolves_001=Passion and Empathy
ResolveCharityWolves_002=For the residents of {townname}, though I shudder at the descriptions of their mongrel countenances, there was deep affection for those thrust into the epic struggle between wild passion and sympathy for the lesser among them. {charity} III's fiery ambitions inspired the beasts, while their familial legacy of humility and charity - begrudgingly or elsewise - garnered an even deeper admiration.
ResolveCharityWolves_003=There was not a day that went by with a friendly set of claws proudly patting their shoulder or saliva - laden greeting at the local pub. As naive as they were, some even relished the opportunity to donate their labors inside the ominous iron gates upon the hillside.
ResolveCharityWolves_004={charity} may **gain a Servant from Lost** (if possible) and **returns their**{icon:creepy_icon}**token to the start of the**{icon:creepy_icon}**Track.**

# passages/00355-MayorLibraryEvil.mws.yaml
MayorLibraryEvil_001=Detestable Education
MayorLibraryEvil_002=It was impossible for {mayor} III to convince them otherwise; for the new leaders of {townname}, access to untamed knowledge had poisoned the pure minds of the citizens. They were well aware that it was {mayor}'s ancestry that had brought this blight of terrible cognition to this fair town.
MayorLibraryEvil_003=For with knowledge came a way to overcome the fears inhabiting the hearts of all men - a fear that could be manipulated. And they bore a deep grudge against anyone that sook to quell that primal urge.
MayorLibraryEvil_004=For with knowledge came a lack of faith; a propensity to question authority and cause unwanted friction. It made them look upon {mayor} III the same way they looked upon the beasts they hunted in the wild.
MayorLibraryEvil_005={mayor} gains 2 {icon:creepy_icon}. Then, return the **Commemorative Mayoral Coin** to the scenario box.

# passages/00356-HelpingEvil2.mws.yaml
HelpingEvil2_001=Then, starting with the player with the **most Victory Points** and continuing in descending order of points, each player with a {society} token chooses a **Master's Study** to build on their Estate. No additional cost is paid for a new plot to place this tile. _(Ties are broken by the player that went later in turn order in the previous round.) Return all unclaimed tiles to the box._

# passages/00357-WolvesSetupGen3.mws.yaml
WolvesSetupGen3_001=Each player retrieves a **Storybook token** and places it on their Masterwork.
WolvesSetupGen3_002=_When a player completes their Masterwork, they will consult the Storybook for a special message from the Order._

# passages/00358-HospitalVisitReject.mws.yaml
HospitalVisitReject_001=Kind Rejection
HospitalVisitReject_002=Legal proceedings were still ongoing due to their previous visit to the Hospital grounds. Therefore, Dr. {hospsign}'s repeated presence was not well-received by the staff nor by the other cousins who were forced to witness them debase themselves by raising their voice and trying to forcefully gain entry to the facility.
HospitalVisitReject_003=Was it madness that drove them to it or a deep obsession that even this humble biographer cannot fathom? Whatever mental deficiency urged them onward, it certainly did not have the desired outcome.
HospitalVisitReject_004=Gain 1 {icon:creepy_icon}.

# passages/00359-WolvesBankMayorGood.mws.yaml
WolvesBankMayorGood_001=The Stench of Man's Avarice
WolvesBankMayorGood_002=These beastly apparitions may have squashed their hirsute forms into makeshift suits and summer dresses - photographs of which degrade the very silver they were impressed upon - but when the subject of money was discussed, they sneered in disgust.
WolvesBankMayorGood_003=For they abhored all forms of numismatic pursuits, only abiding them as a necessity in their brief business dealings with the outside world. {mayor} III's family lineage bore the golden mark of this shameful greed, and set their noses twitching every time they entered {townname}'s limits.
WolvesBankMayorGood_004={mayor} gains 1 {icon:creepy_icon} and loses **2VP**. Then, return the **Commemorative Mayoral Coin** to the scenario box.

